MFEM mesh v1.0

# This is a carefully designed mesh consisting of wedge and pyramid
# elements. The arrangement of elements was designed to explore a wide
# variety of element interface orientations.
#
# For example, the mesh contains:
# - neighboring wedge elements with a shared triangular face
# - two pairs of neighboring wedge elements with shared
#   quadrilateral faces with the z-component of their reference spaces
#   aligned and misaligned
# - aligned/misaligned configurations of pyramids with a shared triangular face
# - neighboring pyramids with a shared quadrilateral face
# - mixed wedge/pyramid pairs with a shared triangular face
# - mixed wedge/pyramid pairs with a shared quadrilateral face
#
# The possible relative orientations are not exhaustive but they cover many
# important cases involving alignment/misalignment of the z-coordinates of
# the respective reference spaces.
#
# The mesh also happens to be reminiscent of the LLNL logo.

#
# MFEM Geometry Types (see fem/geom.hpp):
#
# POINT       = 0
# SEGMENT     = 1
# TRIANGLE    = 2
# SQUARE      = 3
# TETRAHEDRON = 4
# CUBE        = 5
# PRISM       = 6
# PYRAMID     = 7
#

